<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/reactive/store',
        '/handlers/post',
        '/ambients/config',
        '/app/environment',
        '/reactive/refresh',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/database.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('each migration runs once, in order, across boots over one file",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/TargetLog.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a target set is a row in the file, listed newest first'"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Keep the team's targets through a restart">
        <p>The first call opens <code>crm.sqlite</code> in <code>APP_DATA_DIR</code> and runs
            the migrations it has not run. Every call after hands back the same
            <code>bun:sqlite</code> <code>Database</code>.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { database } from '@abide/abide/server'

            export const crmDatabase = database('crm', {
                migrations: [
                    \`CREATE TABLE targets (
                        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
                        target INTEGER NOT NULL
                    )\`,
                    'CREATE TABLE digests (sentAt INTEGER NOT NULL)',
                ],
            })

            crmDatabase().query('INSERT INTO targets (target) VALUES (?)').run(250_000)
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Add a column with one more migration">
        <p>Append to the list and never edit a migration already shipped. A function seeds rows
            on the boot that runs it.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { database } from '@abide/abide/server'

            export const crmDatabase = database('crm', {
                migrations: [
                    \`CREATE TABLE targets (
                        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
                        target INTEGER NOT NULL
                    )\`,
                    'CREATE TABLE digests (sentAt INTEGER NOT NULL)',
                    'ALTER TABLE targets ADD COLUMN quarter TEXT',
                    (db) => db.run('INSERT INTO targets (target) VALUES (100000)'),
                ],
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Open the file the config names">
        <p>A function names the file as it opens, so it reads the config of that moment. A name
            holding a <code>/</code> or a <code>.</code> is a path.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { config, database } from '@abide/abide/server'

            export const notes = database(() => config().NOTES_DB as string, {
                migrations: ['CREATE TABLE notes (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, body TEXT)'],
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Refresh pages when a script writes the database file">
        <p><code>changed</code> counts commits from other connections, such as the
            <code>sqlite3</code> shell or a second server, and never the opener's own. On the
            server a bare <code>refresh</code> reloads every <code>global</code> value and every
            value a browser follows.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { refresh, watch } from '@abide/abide'
            import { crmDatabase } from './lib/crmDatabase.server.ts'

            watch(() => {
                crmDatabase.changed()
                refresh()
            })
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
